,"color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-09-11T03:11:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T05:22:34Z","closed_at":"2025-09-11T23:38:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1, 4.5.beta7, 4.5.rc2 \n- Not reproducible in: 4.3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Linux Mint 21.3 (Virginia) - X11 - GLES3 (Compatibility) - REMBRANDT (rembrandt, LLVM 15.0.7, DRM 3.42, 5.15.0-151-generic) - AMD Ryzen 5 PRO 6650U with Radeon Graphics (12 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm using an AnimationTree to control the animations for an AnimatedSprite2D using an AnimationPlayer. I have a state machine as the root node and I'm using BlendSpace2D nodes as the leaf nodes so I can set the animation based on the direction of the player by setting the blend_space parameter to match the player's normalised movement vector. After upgrading to the 4.5 beta I found that setting the blend_space parameter doesn't change the animation.\n\nIn my original project I found that the animation changes eventually (after one or more seconds of holding a different direction) but couldn't reproduce that in an MRP.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing the MRP:\n1) Move the character around using the arrow keys.\n\nExpected behaviour (seen in 4.3):\n* The animation changes when changing direction.\n\nActual behaviour (seen in 4.4.1 and later):\n* The animation doesn't change.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test-blendspace2d.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22267035/test-blendspace2d.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node